cff-version: 1.2.0
title: ThermophysicalDB.jl
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the
  metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Eduardo Bader Dalfovo Mohr
    family-names: Alves
    email: eduardo.alves@polo.ufsc.br
repository-code: "https://github.com/Eduardo-BDMAlves/ThermophysicalDB.jl"
url: "https://eduardo-bdmalves.github.io/ThermophysicalDB.jl/stable"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A Julia package that downloads, caches and queries experimental thermophysical
  property data from public databases, starting with the NIST/TRC ThermoML Archive.
  The package does not contain or redistribute any data.
# The works this package credits. Every entry has an `abbreviation`, its citation key in the
# form of the reference manager (surname of the first author, year, first word of the title,
# all lower case), and `keywords`:
#   data-source  credited in every file exported from the data of the database
#   group        work of the research group, for the documentation
#   background   other reading about the data, for the documentation
# `ThermophysicalDB.check_references()` verifies the keys and compares the articles with the
# DOI resolver. The notice, the exported `.bib` files and the bibliography of the
# documentation are all generated from this list.
references:
